From 3c353e87c39abb2d0b3296fc8e7ba40fa20dd8e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:28:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): preserve own-turn switches and one-shot refusal
 semantics [daveey]

Review rework: a model switch on an external RPC thread must not replace a running turn's runtime, but the executing turn must retain its deliberate Nous wire transition. Reuse the existing local origin custody scope, live holder and execution-thread identity for the exemption; copied contexts and stale thread IDs confer no authority. Both managed staged and unmanaged in-place branches retain the admission lock.

MoA one-shots refuse a lost admission race instead of replaying as a permanent pin. Stage their restore locally until success, preserving an existing turn's restore on a failed second command. Propagate deferred reset results rather than reporting reset_done, and acknowledge the exact stash result rather than an older pending pick.

Proof: all four independent reviewer probes failed on 0ec450a4d7. The new real-facade own-turn cases fail 2/2 without the exemption and pass with it; the same cases reject copied-context foreign threads. Final managed-switch and gateway regressions: 42 passed across five files. Expanded consumer run: 5076 passed, 2 skipped across 286 files. scripts/check: all 21 checks passed. New exact-head CI and independent review remain mandatory before canonical ship lands this head.

Hermes-Card: t_eeeeee0000000032
